{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  THE FIRST PURCHASE, named.

  A customer who has just met the brand does not want to choose between six
  bottles they have never tasted; they want to be told where to start. On
  desktop the Sets carousel does that job with room to browse. On a phone it is
  a second horizontal rail immediately after the first one, and the two read as
  the same thing twice.

  So this is the mobile answer: ONE set, presented as the recommended way in,
  with the carousel left exactly as it is on desktop. The section hides itself
  above the mobile breakpoint — display:none rather than a visual hide, so a
  screen reader on a wide viewport is not offered the same set twice.

  EVERYTHING NUMERIC COMES FROM SHOPIFY. Price, compare-at price and
  availability are read off the product on every render. Nothing here is a
  setting a merchant could leave stale, which is the whole point: a hardcoded
  "$150" survives a price change and lies about it.

  The saving line only appears when compare_at_price is genuinely higher than
  price. It is not derived, assumed, or written by hand — if Shopify does not
  say there is a saving, the page does not claim one.

  The body copy IS a setting, because it describes what is in the box and only
  a person who knows the box should be writing that.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign p = section.settings.product
  assign v = p.selected_or_first_available_variant
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  THE WHOLE SECTION, not just its contents.

  Hiding .non-firstbuy in the stylesheet left the section WRAPPER in the
  document — a zero-height div between Made for and Poured at on every desktop
  page. It changed nothing visible, and it still showed up in the desktop
  regression diff as a seventh child of `main` where there had been six, which
  is exactly the kind of "harmless" difference that makes a diff stop being
  trusted.

  Written here rather than in theme.css because the wrapper's id is generated
  and only the section itself knows it — the same reason mobile_order writes
  its rule here. Above the breakpoint the section is not in the layout at all.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  @media (min-width: 860px) {
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} { display: none; }
  }
</style>

{%- if p != blank -%}
  <div class="non-firstbuy" data-non-firstbuy>
    <div class="non-firstbuy__copy">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}
        <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <h2 class="non-firstbuy__title">{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>

      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <p class="non-firstbuy__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="non-firstbuy__price">
        {%- if p.available -%}
          <span class="non-firstbuy__now">{{ p.price | money }}</span>
          {%- comment -%}
            Strictly greater than. `!= blank` would print a strike-through on
            every product where compare_at equals price, which is most of them,
            and a crossed-out identical number reads as a discount that is not
            there.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if p.compare_at_price > p.price -%}
            <s class="non-firstbuy__was">{{ p.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
            {%- assign saving = p.compare_at_price | minus: p.price -%}
            <span class="non-firstbuy__save">
              {{ section.settings.save_word }} {{ saving | money }}
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- else -%}
          <span class="non-firstbuy__now">{{ 'products.product.sold_out' | t }}</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      <div class="non-firstbuy__actions">
        {%- comment -%}
          A LINK TO THE PRODUCT, not an add-to-cart.

          A six-bottle set is a considered purchase and it has variants; adding
          the first available one from a homepage band would be choosing on the
          customer's behalf. The PDP is two taps from here and shows what they
          are buying.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if p.available -%}
          <a class="non-btn non-firstbuy__cta" href="{{ p.url }}">
            {{ section.settings.cta_label }}
          </a>
        {%- else -%}
          <a class="non-btn non-btn--ghost non-firstbuy__cta" href="{{ p.url }}">
            {{ section.settings.sold_out_cta }}
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if section.settings.link_label != blank and section.settings.link_url != blank -%}
          <a class="non-firstbuy__more" href="{{ section.settings.link_url }}">
            {{ section.settings.link_label }} &rarr;
          </a>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if p.featured_image != blank -%}
      <a class="non-firstbuy__media" href="{{ p.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
        {{
          p.featured_image
          | image_url: width: 800, format: 'webp'
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            widths: '320,480,640,800',
            sizes: '(min-width: 860px) 0px, 45vw',
            class: 'non-firstbuy__img',
            alt: ''
        }}
      </a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Inside the guard: with no product configured there is no band, and nothing
    for the script to observe or report on.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <script src="{{ 'featured-set.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Featured set",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "product",
      "label": "The set",
      "info": "Price, saving and availability are read from this product every time the page renders. Nothing is copied here."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "New to NON?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Start with the Mixed 6 Pack."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Body",
      "default": "Six bottles across the range — the simplest way to find what belongs on your table.",
      "info": "Describes what is in the box. Change it if the set changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Button",
      "default": "Shop the Mixed 6 Pack"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "sold_out_cta",
      "label": "Button when sold out",
      "default": "See the set"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "save_word",
      "label": "Saving word",
      "default": "Save"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "link_label",
      "label": "Secondary link label",
      "default": "View all sets"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "id": "link_url",
      "label": "Secondary link"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Featured set"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
